@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
}

<div class="px-4 py-5 my-3 text-center">
    <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold">Provider Management</h1>
    <div class="col-lg-8 mx-auto">
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Manage state-licensed providers and their licenses. Built with ASP.NET Core MVC,
            EF Core, and SQLite, with soft-delete enforced at the database, query, and
            interceptor layers.
        </p>
        <div class="d-grid gap-2 d-sm-flex justify-content-sm-center">
            <a asp-controller="Dashboard" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg px-4 gap-3">
                Open Dashboard
            </a>
            <a asp-controller="Providers" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-lg px-4">
                Browse Providers
            </a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mt-5">
    <div class="col-md-4">
        <h4>Soft-delete by design</h4>
        <p>Hard deletion is disallowed by policy. Providers and licenses are flagged
           IsDeleted, hidden from standard queries, and remain queryable for audit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-4">
        <h4>Audit-safe</h4>
        <p>Deleted records are visible from the <a asp-controller="Providers" asp-action="Deleted">Audit page</a>
           and can be restored. Cascade soft-delete keeps parent and child records in sync.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-4">
        <h4>Architectural separation</h4>
        <p>Domain, Infrastructure, Services, and Web layers are split by folder. Controllers
           depend on services; services depend on repositories; repositories own EF Core.</p>
    </div>
</div>
